Some NPCs only exchange Crowns for goods and services, these are:

* [[Sev]], the Dye Vendor, exchanging 1 Crown per [[Dye Packet]], or 25 Crowns for the Manycolored Equipment unlock, allowing free and infinite dye usage on ''equipment''.
* [[Sordino]] the Tamer of Beasts, exchanging the [[Mounts|Thresher Mount]] for 3 Crowns.
* While [[Traan Zakshun]] sells goods for Notes normally, his Black Market wares are sold exclusively for Crowns.

Note that currently, the Crown system is being slowly rolled out, meaning more uses/trades for Crowns are to be expected.

=='''Trivia'''==
*Due to it's relatively low difficulty, fighting the [[Scion of Ethiron]] can be a great way to farm Crowns for people who can't fight the [[Heart of Enmity]] or don't want to wait for World Events. Otherwise, if you are ready to wait for World Events, [[The Doom of Caeranthil]] is the best option as you can join another server with the boss after killing one, giving 4-12 Crowns, if you are fast enough.
**If you want to kill [[The Doom of Caeranthil]] faster, you can buy [[Ships & Sailing|Schooner]] and "alternate" between two cannons at the front of a ship by quickly taking the second cannon after shooting from the first one. This also will allow you to contribute more damage if you're not alone, rewarding you more Crowns.
*Crown are one of two currencies that can be interacted with by clicking their icons, the other being [[Notes]].
**Clicking Crowns allows you to exchange them for Notes/Knowledge, while clicking Notes allows you to drop up to 1000 Notes at a time.
