==Interface==
There are 11 interface related settings.
*'''Cinematic Mode {{Input|input|On/Off}}''' - "Hides the UI for screenshots and videos."
**Does not hide player list or [[Teleportation]] markers.
*'''Hide Names {{Input|input|On/Off}}''' - "Hides character names."
**Hides the names of other players in-game from your PoV.
**Does not hide your own or others in the player list or top info bar.
*'''Cooldown Bars {{Input|input|On/Off}}''' - "Enables cooldown indicator bars."
**Cooldown Bars will appear whenever an effect is procced, indicating when it is able to proc again.
*'''Stat Bar Behavior {{Input|input|Always/Hover}}''' - "Sets when your stat bars shows their percentages."
**Always: Percentages on Posture, Health, Armor, Natural Armor, Ether, Tempo, Heartfire, and Specter bars will be displayed in text at all times.
**Hover (default): The percentages on the above will only be displayed when hovering over the bar with your mouse.
**Does not work on Blood, Food, and Hunger.
**Note: Being hit by a [[Harrowing]] Enchanted weapon will hide the percentages for the duration of the effect. If this setting is set to "Always", then the percentages will not come back until you die, leave the game, or re-toggle the setting.
*'''Crafting Slots {{Input|input|On/Off}}''' - "Displays 3 slots for Crafting above your Backpack."
**Drag items and materials into the 3 slots to craft from your inventory without Journal recipes.
**Some crafting recipes (namely [[Enchant Stone]]s and [[Enchant Grease|Grease]] do not work with the crafting slots, and need to be crafted in your journal.
*'''Points of Interest {{Input|input|On/Off}}''' - "Enables markers in towns for points of interest."
**When On: Displays markers for [[Antiquarian]]s (including the [[Antiques Smuggler]]), [[Attunement Trainer]]s, [[Banker]]s, [[Blacksmith]]s, [[Combat Training]] entrance NPC, [[Dungeons|Dungeon]] entrances, [[Food]] vendors, [[Gear Cabinet]]s, [[Guildhall]] NPCs, [[Inn]] Keepers, [[Job Boards]], [[Mantra Lectern]]s, and [[Shipwright]]s in the physical world. These can be seen through walls.
**These markers are displaysd on the [[Maps|Map]], regardless if setting is on or off.
**[[Guild Bases|Guild Base]] NPCs/Mantra Lectern do not have the Point of Interest displays.
*'''3D Icon Behavior {{Input|input|Always/Hover/Off}}''' - "Sets 3D icon behavior."
**Always: Displays the 3D models of applicable items inside of the inventory and hotbar, instead of their item name.
**Hover: When hovering your mouse over items in your hotbar or inventory, the 3D model of applicable items will be displayed instead of the item's name.
**Off (default): Items in your inventory and hotbar will always display their name instead of their 3D models.
*'''Show Buff Pips {{Input|input|On/Off}}''' - "Shows buff pips on equipment without needing to hover over them."
**Displays all pip icons on equipment in the inventory, showing their rarity and pip type.
*'''Show Player List {{Input|input|On/Off}}''' - "Toggles the visibility of the player list."
*'''Leave Game Prompt {{Input|input|On/Off}}''' - "Enables the confirmation prompt for returning to Main Menu."
**When On (default): Pressing the "Return to Main Menu" button will show a confirmation prompt, and will only send the player to the menu when they confirm it.
**When Off: Pressing the "Return to Main Menu" button will instantly send the player to the main menu.
*'''Streamer Mode {{Input|input|On/Off}}''' - "Makes it harder for players to find your server."
**When On: Server name, server region, exact server time, and the guilds of players in the playerlist are hidden. Additionally, hovering over player names on the server list will not display their usernames.

==Audio==
There are 6 audio related settings.
*'''Master Volume {{Input|input|Slider 0-100}}''' - "Adjust the overall volume of the game. Does not currently apply to every sound, this is being worked on!"
*'''Music Volume {{Input|input|Slider 0-100}}''' - "Adjust the volume of ambient music tracks."
*'''Weather Volume {{Input|input|Slider 0-100}}''' - "Adjust the volume of weather effects."
*'''Sound Effects Volume {{Input|input|Slider 0-100}}''' - "Adjust the volume of most sound effects."
*'''Instruments Volume {{Input|input|Slider 0-100}}''' - "Adjust the volume of musical instruments heard in the world."
*'''Voice Volume {{Input|input|Slider 0-100}}''' - "Adjust the volume of other players' voices."

==Graphics==
There are 5 graphics related settings.
*'''Low Graphics Mode {{Input|input|On/Off}}''' - "Lowers particle counts and reduces the fidelity on various other visuals."
*'''Cloth Physics {{Input|input|On/Off}}''' - "Enables physically simulated animations for equipment."
**When On (default): Eligible equipment items will gain physics, and will move as the player does.
*'''Field of View {{Input|input|Slider 50-85}}''' - "Adjusts the default camera FoV."
*'''Dynamic FoV {{Input|input|On/Off}}''' - "Dynamically adjusts your FoV based on your speed."
**When On: As the player speeds up and moves faster, the FoV will be increased, zooming out the camera.
*'''Camera Smoothing {{Input|input|On/Off}}''' - "Smooths out camera and focuses on torso movement."
**When On: The camera will slightly adjust to the positioning of the player's torso, instead of remaining at one spot.

==Combat==
There are 8 combat related settings.
*'''No Holds Barred {{Input|input|On/Off}}''' - "Disables ally checks for abilities."
**When On: Your allies will temporarily no longer count as your allies in all aspects. You will combat eachother when attacking, be able to target eachother with attacks, ally-exclusive buffs will no longer work, etc.
**When turning this setting on, or when your character spawns while this setting is on, they'll say one of two quoted: "I [[Glossary#Vows|Vow]] to fight with no holds barred." or "I [[Glossary#Vows|Vow]] to not hold back."
**When turning this setting off, your character will say one of two quotes: "Fight's over." or "Show's over."
*'''Hold to Attack {{Input|input|On/Off}}''' - "Lets you hold your Basic Attack input to automatically swing."
**When On: Holding M1 will repeatedly swing your weapon back-to-back.
*'''Input Buffering {{Input|input|On/Off}}''' - "Enables input buffering on your Basic Attacks."
*'''Mantra Buffering {{Input|input|On/Off}}''' - "Enables input buffering on your Mantras when you miss your Basic Attacks."
*'''Preload Animations {{Input|input|On/Off}}''' - "Most player and mob animations will be loaded as soon as you enter the game."
**This may increase load times.
*'''Disable Enemy Vanity {{Input|input|On/Off}}''' - "Hides enemy equipment."
*'''Hide Spell Shouts {{Input|input|On/Off}}''' - "Disables spell shout visibility."
**When On: The text from the {{t|Spell Shout}} Talent will be hidden.
**This does not affect {{t|Unnecessary Theatrics}} or {{t|Heretic's Sutra}}.
*'''Simple Telegraphs {{Input|input|On/Off}}''' - "Telegraphs only show an outline over the character and don't emit any particles."
**When On: [[Combat Mechanics#Telegraphs|Attack telegraphs]] will be displayed solely as a colored outline on the character, rather than displaying the glyph.

==Network==
There are 2 network related settings.
*'''Preferred Region {{Input|input|Any/West NA/East NA/Europe/Asia/Oceania/South America}}''' - "Which region you'd like to be matchmaked into for different gamemodes. Not guaranteed.
*'''Ping Compensation {{Input|input|On/Off}}''' - "Delays incoming damage slightly to help you react."

==Accessibility==
There are 3 accessibility related settings.
*'''Photosensitive Mode {{Input|input|On/Off}}''' - "Reduces the intensity of certain visual effects."
*'''Unlocked Sprinting {{Input|input|On/Off}}''' - "While sprinting in Camera Lock, face your movement direction."
**When On: While shift-lock is active, your character will face their movement direction while sprinting. This can make certain parkour actions, like wall-jumping, significantly more difficult.
**When Off: While shift-lock is active, your character will face forwards while sprinting. This allows you to strafe in any direction, including backwards.
*'''Sprint Input Behavior {{Input|input|Hold/Toggle}}''' - "Change whether you have to hold the sprint input, or whether you toggle it with each input."

==Trivia==
*For a very brief period of time on the October 5th, 2025 update, there was a setting called "Auto-Vault." This allowed the player to automatically vault over obstacles while sprinting.

