==Description==
Ten is the central figure behind the island [[Simforea]] and the disappearance of the [[Anansi]] race. They were an exceptionally ambitious [[Anansi]] and the only known member of their race to awaken ten eyes, far beyond the six eyes Anansi traditionally sought through meditation.<ref>{{Ref/Bestiary|Knell, The Lost Anansi}}</ref> They created an organ and cradle designed to draw souls from the [[Moonseye]] and inject them into their body.<ref name="Manuscript">Manuscripts found within [[Simforea]]</ref>

Ten's experiment ultimately destroyed them. Their body could not withstand the souls they absorbed, causing them to mutate and develop increasingly more eyes until they lost control of their body.<ref name="Manuscript" /> Their experiments also caused Simforea to deteriorate.<ref name="Remnant">[[Remnants of Soul]] description</ref> Ten later lured the other Anansi to Simforea, and Ten's supernatural connection to them allowed them to sense the success of his cradle and follow him there. This ultimately led to the disappearance and death of the Anansi race.<ref name="Manuscript" /><ref name="Remnant" />

Along all of this, Ten encountered [[Knell, The Lunatic Resonator|Knell]] and promised him that he would finally obtain a [[Resonance]].<ref>{{Ref/NPC|Knell, The Lunatic Resonator|quote= You're BEAMING-BEAMING with ripples of stolen inheritance. Maybe your soul... no. Your mind's the key! THE KEY! The key!!! Key to the mending of my wretched, discordant, SCREAMING soul... the sight Ten promised us.}}</ref>

